  "text": "And some copies aren't copies. Northwind stores a price on each product, and another on every order line. Six hundred sixty-two lines disagree, and they're RIGHT. Prices rose, and each line kept what the customer paid. Two facts that share a name. A copy needs syncing. History needs nobody to ever fix it.\n\nSo, normalize first, denormalize on purpose, and keep every copy in sync. Knowing the rules is half of it. The other half is a process for using them, and for changing a design once it's live.",
